## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/segmentbyvalue.html
- Summary (EN): Segment by Value takes a mono layer and outputs an ID layer in which pixels with similar values share an ID. It forms a series of iso-contours, even between pixels that are not connected.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Segment by Value transforme une couche mono en couche d'identifiants, où les pixels de valeurs voisines partagent le même numéro.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the mono layer to segment"]

- Key parameters: ["Method: Width and Offset, or Number of Segments", "Width: maximum value difference inside one segment (Width and Offset method)", "Offset: where the first segment starts (Width and Offset method)", "Segments: number of segments between the minimum and maximum values (Number of Segments method)", "Segment Location: Starts at Value (floor) or Centered at Value (round)", "Minimum Value / Maximum Value: input range; a dropper can set them from the layer", "Values Below / Values Above: Extend, Invalid (-1), Clamp or Wrap"]

- Caveats: ["Several parameters apply to one method only", "With Invalid (-1), out-of-range pixels receive the explicit segment ID -1", "The page does not state default parameter values"]

